diff --git a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
index 6bddff1..14d006c 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
@@ -96,3 +96,46 @@ __Request:__
 __Response:__
 
 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
+## `POST /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions`
+
+Registers the browser push subscription for the current device. You can only register a subscription for yourself. Posting the same endpoint again updates the keys.
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `endpoint` | string | Yes | Push service endpoint from the browser subscription |
+| `p256dh_key` | string | Yes | Client public key (`keys.p256dh`) |
+| `auth_key` | string | Yes | Client auth secret (`keys.auth`) |
+
+__Request:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "push_subscription": {
+    "endpoint": "https://push.example/subscription",
+    "p256dh_key": "client-public-key",
+    "auth_key": "client-auth-secret"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the subscription id.
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5va03bpuvkcjemcxl73ho2",
+  "endpoint": "https://push.example/subscription"
+}
+```
+
+When a notification lands in the tray, Fizzy sends a web push to each of the user's subscriptions. The payload title and body match the tray, and `url` opens the card the notification is about. Sending requires `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`.
+
+## `DELETE /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions/:id`
+
+Removes a push subscription for the current user.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `204 No Content` on success.
